   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The functions \\( f \\) and \\( g \\) are differentiable, with \\( f(4) = -4 \\), \\( f'(4) = 2 \\), \\( g(4) = 3 \\), \\( g'(4) = 2 \\). Let \\( h(x) = f(x)g(x) \\). Find the value of \\( h'(4) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -2
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Record the values at \\( x = 4 \\): \\( f(4) = -4 \\), \\( f'(4) = 2 \\), \\( g(4) = 3 \\), \\( g'(4) = 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule, \\( (fg)'(4) = f'(4)g(4) + f(4)g'(4) \\).",
         "mathjson": -4
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute: \\( (2)(3) + (-4)(2) = -2 \\).",
         "mathjson": -2
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( h'(4) = -2 \\).",
         "mathjson": -2
      }
   ],
